  "version": 1,
  "title": "Regular subgraphs of almost regular graphs (Alon–Friedland–Kalai)",
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the Alon–Friedland–Kalai theorem for primes: for a prime p, every finite simple graph with maximum degree at most 2p − 1 and average degree greater than 2p − 2 contains a p-regular subgraph (a nonempty subgraph with all degrees 0 or p); as a corollary, every 4-regular graph plus an edge contains a 3-regular subgraph. The prime-power case of the paper is not stated. The proof uses Mathlib's Chevalley–Warning theorem.",
